<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Damme</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Damme is a small town in West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruges">Bruges</a>. Founded in the late twelfth century on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zwin">Zwin</a> inlet, it served as the outport of Bruges, where goods passed between sea-going ships and the city. In 1213 an English fleet destroyed the French fleet of Philip II Augustus in its harbour. The silting of the Zwin ended its trade, leaving a well-preserved small medieval town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/damme.jpg" alt="Damme" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Pol GRANDMONT · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:0_Damme_-_Stadhuis_(1).JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
